{"schema": 1, "kind": "review", "id": "rev-20261109T221641Z-a46ae6bc", "ts": "2026-11-09T22:20:22Z", "actor": {"worktree": "arrt", "plugin": "3.8.1-dev", "branch": "feature/watches", "build": "52bb14851a37"}, "body": {"base_commit": "08a4a77031ed5d725e7dd78c3164364d508933fa", "base_tree": "b5d3bf9b0a2246fb344880487731a99bf720b2a8", "head_tree": "ce1a8589fc753f8e32e8259a4427c99acdcbe673", "head_commit": null, "dispatch_commit": "8e4eab544f9f773274cbbb92fa725fb61a2e70ce", "mode": "final (full review, ready for push)", "mode_chosen_by": "explicit-args", "stage": "inner", "tier": "escalate", "roster": [{"role": "correctness", "model": "claude-opus-5-5"}, {"role": "design", "model": "claude-opus-5-5"}, {"role": "sustainability", "model": "claude-opus-5-5"}], "files_reviewed": ["arrt/src/arrt/__main__.py", "arrt/src/arrt/app.py", "arrt/src/arrt/http/static/screens/activity.js", "arrt/src/arrt/library/discovery/engine.py", "arrt/src/arrt/library/discovery/openrouter.py", "arrt/src/arrt/library/discovery/phase_one.py", "arrt/src/arrt/library/services/discovery.py", "arrt/src/arrt/library/services/runner.py", "arrt/src/arrt/library/services/scheduler.py", "arrt/src/arrt/library/services/unattended.py", "arrt/src/arrt/library/services/watches.py", "arrt/src/arrt/services/container.py", "arrt/tests/integration/test_watches_surface.py", "arrt/tests/unit/test_scheduler.py", "arrt/tests/unit/test_watches.py"], "files_changed": [".prawduct/artifacts/build-plan-watches.md", ".prawduct/artifacts/data-model.md", "arrt/src/arrt/__main__.py", "arrt/src/arrt/app.py", "arrt/src/arrt/http/static/screens/activity.js", "arrt/src/arrt/library/discovery/engine.py", "arrt/src/arrt/library/discovery/openrouter.py", "arrt/src/arrt/library/discovery/phase_one.py", "arrt/src/arrt/library/services/discovery.py", "arrt/src/arrt/library/services/runner.py", "arrt/src/arrt/library/services/scheduler.py", "arrt/src/arrt/library/services/unattended.py", "arrt/src/arrt/library/services/watches.py", "arrt/src/arrt/services/container.py", "arrt/tests/integration/test_watches_surface.py", "arrt/tests/unit/test_scheduler.py", "arrt/tests/unit/test_watches.py"], "files_oracle": [".prawduct/artifacts/build-plan-watches.md", ".prawduct/artifacts/data-model.md"], "findings": [{"goal": "Nothing Is Broken", "severity": "blocking", "title": "The unattended model's path to the provider is untested past the scripted engine", "recommendation": "Two changed lines have no test: phase_one.py passes `model=request.model` to the client, and openrouter.py sends `\"model\": self._model if model is None else model` in the request body. The only check is test_scheduler.py asserting `engine.requests[-1].model` on the scripted engine, which sits above both lines. Delete `model=request.model` from OpenRouterEngine.work_list, or send `self._model` unconditionally, and every suite stays green while each Watch quietly runs on the default discovery model. Core learning 'When a behaviour matters because something calls or reads it, test through that caller with a non-default value and mutate the lines you changed'. Add two tests. (a) test_phase_one_engine: a WorkListRequest with a non-default model reaches the client's request body. (b) test_openrouter_client: `complete(model=...)` puts that model in the captured body, and `model=None` keeps the client's own. Watch each fail once against a re-break. Scope: instance.", "files": ["arrt/src/arrt/library/discovery/phase_one.py", "arrt/src/arrt/library/discovery/openrouter.py", "arrt/tests/unit/test_scheduler.py"], "fid": "R-1"}, {"goal": "Nothing Is Missing", "severity": "blocking", "title": "Only one of the 'did not finish' statuses is tested for retry-soon", "recommendation": "Chunk 04's test list asks for 'a run of each failure kind is retried at the next pass, not in a loop'. `_DID_NOT_FINISH` holds FAILED, INTERRUPTED and HALTED_BY_BUDGET, but only FAILED is exercised (test_a_finished_run_waits_its_cadence_and_a_failed_one_an_hour_not_a_pass). Nothing tests that CANCELLED waits the full interval. Remove INTERRUPTED or HALTED_BY_BUDGET from the frozenset, or add CANCELLED, and the suite stays green. INTERRUPTED is the restart case the plan singles out. Fix: parametrise the retry test over every member of `_DID_NOT_FINISH`, using the symbol rather than a hand-copied list. Add one CANCELLED case, plus one COMPLETED case already partly present, asserting the full-cadence wait. Scope: instance.", "files": ["arrt/src/arrt/library/services/watches.py", "arrt/tests/unit/test_scheduler.py"], "fid": "R-2"}, {"goal": "Decisions Were Deliberate", "severity": "note", "title": "Learnings cross-check: the deployment's schedule=True is the non-default value through the caller, and it is untested", "recommendation": "Rule cited: 'When a behaviour matters because something calls or reads it, test through that caller with a non-default value'. __main__.main now passes schedule=True, which is the only thing that turns the unattended spender on in a deployment. The plan records it as untested and puts the topic sweep and the queue in the same position, so it is a recorded acceptance and not a regression. An inexpensive way to make it testable: pull the create_app keyword arguments __main__ builds into a function a unit test can call without uvicorn.run. Scope: class (every lifespan flag __main__ sets). Also checked and clean: 'When you delete a constant or add a required parameter, grep tools/ and scripts/' (WatchService's new required `unattended`, the start_discovery_run and complete signatures: arrt/tools has no consumers, and there is no scripts/). 'When a clause or notice is conditional, assert its absence' holds for overdue (the test asserts False while work is off and before a whole cadence has passed). surface.md was read, and no rule there is regressed by this diff.", "files": ["arrt/src/arrt/__main__.py"], "fid": "R-3"}, {"goal": "Decisions Were Deliberate", "severity": "note", "title": "Backlog: #178 (the scheduler) is cited in new code and does not resolve in the backlog cache", "recommendation": "C-B4. `backlog cache-query resolve 178` reports unresolved (cache confirmed 2026-11-09T21:05Z), but scheduler.py's module docstring and the reworded activity.js comment both cite it, and upgrades.md names #178 as 'the scheduler'. It is probably parked or closed, so it is outside the open cache. This chunk builds the scheduler that #178 describes, with Watches as its first job, so what #178 still owes is the upgrades job. Check that #178's body still describes current state and narrow it if not. Do not change its status on this review's say-so. No open item's affected paths cover the changed files (`affecting` returned 0). #417 is open and is closed by d434e17b's 'Closes #417', which is outside this interval and needs nothing here. Scope: instance.", "files": ["arrt/src/arrt/library/services/scheduler.py", "arrt/src/arrt/http/static/screens/activity.js"], "fid": "R-4"}, {"goal": "Decisions Were Deliberate", "severity": "note", "title": "Records Pass: covered both oracle files, and neither clears a bar", "recommendation": "Covered: .prawduct/artifacts/build-plan-watches.md (the five Chunk 04 mid-build decisions and the Chunk 04 section) and .prawduct/artifacts/data-model.md (the Watch last_refusal row, which now lists could_not_start, matching WatchRefusal). Nothing ships a false claim or would mislead an operator into action. Not findings, because they clear no bar: the plan's Observability bullet says 'with a specific catch' while Scheduler.run_pass catches Exception under a waiver, and its Chunk 04 bullet names only failed and interrupted runs as retried at the next hour, while the code also retries halted_by_budget. The record-lint chunk-ref-missing (the plan declares `http/static/screens/activity.js` without the arrt/src/arrt/ prefix) is the Goal 2 holder's to relay, so it is not repeated here. Scope: none.", "fid": "R-5"}], "counts": {"blocking": 2, "warning": 0, "note": 3}, "observations": [{"goal": "Nothing Is Broken", "title": "One pass can start more Watches than the allowance covers", "recommendation": "WatchJob._refusal calls `UnattendedAllowance.standing(estimate)` per Watch. Its `spent_this_month()` counts only billed spend rows, and a run started earlier in the same pass, or still in flight from an earlier pass, has none yet. So with an allowance for one run and N Watches due together (all newly created, or a set of hourly ones), all N start. Unattended spend then overshoots by up to (N-1) estimates. The module's 'a run already under way may finish past it' covers a run that was under way when the check ran. It does not obviously cover starting new runs in the same breath. Fix: have the pass reserve the estimate of each run it starts, and ideally of in-flight unattended runs, before checking the next Watch. Pin it with a test: two due Watches, an allowance for one, expect PassResult(started=1, refused=1). Scope: instance.", "files": ["arrt/src/arrt/library/services/scheduler.py", "arrt/src/arrt/library/services/unattended.py"], "oid": "O-1"}, {"goal": "Nothing Is Broken", "title": "Spend falls back to the client's default model when a per-call model was given", "recommendation": "complete_thread now takes a per-call `model`, but `_read_completion(payload, fallback_model=self._model)` still falls back to the client's own model. A response with no `model` field therefore books a Watch's spend row under the default discovery model rather than the unattended model it actually asked. Fix: pass `fallback_model=self._model if model is None else model`. Scope: instance.", "files": ["arrt/src/arrt/library/discovery/openrouter.py"], "oid": "O-2"}, {"goal": "Nothing Is Missing", "title": "record_lint chunk-ref-missing comes from the path's form, not a missing deliverable", "recommendation": "record_lint reports Chunk 04's declared deliverable `http/static/screens/activity.js` as missing. The deliverable exists and is in this diff, at arrt/src/arrt/http/static/screens/activity.js. The plan wrote the path relative to the package, while the same chunk writes `arrt/src/arrt/library/services/scheduler.py` in full. Nothing was dropped. Fix: write the full repo-relative path in the plan bullet so the lint resolves it. Scope: instance.", "files": [".prawduct/artifacts/build-plan-watches.md"], "oid": "O-3"}, {"goal": "Nothing Is Broken", "title": "Most standing sentences are unasserted", "recommendation": "The suite asserts three of `_sentence`'s outcomes: the OFF refusal, 'Running now.' and the 'Overdue' prefix. The other `_REFUSED` sentences, every `_LAST_RUN` entry, and the 'Not run yet' and 'Off' branches have no assertion. Chunk 05's screen and tool will show these to the household. Parametrise over `WatchRefusal` and over the `_LAST_RUN` keys, so a status or refusal added later fails by name. A refusal would otherwise raise KeyError, and an unknown stored `last_refusal` would raise ValueError in `WatchRefusal(...)`. Scope: instance.", "files": ["arrt/src/arrt/library/services/watches.py", "arrt/tests/unit/test_scheduler.py"], "oid": "O-4"}, {"goal": "The Design Is Sound", "title": "A Watch's run on the unattended model is gated by an estimate priced for the discovery model", "recommendation": "Scope: class. Why it broke: the model became a per-call value, but the price that gates the call did not. `DiscoverySettings.phase1_estimate_usd` is built from `input_cost_usd_per_mtok`/`output_cost_usd_per_mtok`, the discovery model's prices, and its docstring claims it is a bound a run 'physically cannot exceed'. `WatchJob` passes that figure to `UnattendedAllowance.standing(...)` and to the cap check, then starts the run on `UNATTENDED_MODEL`. If the household picks a pricier unattended model, both the allowance and the cap let through a run whose real ceiling is higher, and `run.started` logs `estimated_cost_usd` for a model the run is not using. The plan's Chunk 04 decision says 'nothing else differs', and the price is something that does differ. Fix: price phase 1 per model, so `estimate` takes the model, or refuse an unattended model the deployment has no prices for. Either way, record the choice in place of the 'nothing else differs' premise. While doing it, drop the separate `estimate=lambda: discovery_settings.phase1_estimate_usd` wiring: `WatchJob` already holds the runner, and `runner.estimate()` returns the same figure from one place. To bound the class, search for every reader of the `DiscoverySettings` token prices that can now see a non-default `model`.", "files": ["arrt/src/arrt/library/services/scheduler.py", "arrt/src/arrt/services/container.py", "arrt/src/arrt/library/services/runner.py"], "oid": "O-5"}, {"goal": "The Design Is Sound", "title": "No reservation for started-but-unbilled runs: several Watches due in one pass are each checked against the same billed spend", "recommendation": "Scope: class. Why: the gate has no record of money already committed. `UnattendedAllowance.standing(estimate)` and `spent_by_watch_this_month` read only spend rows that have been billed, and a run's spend is billed when its phase 1 finishes. `WatchJob.run_pass` starts each due Watch in turn, and every check sees the same `spent`. So N Watches with a little more than one estimate of allowance left all start, overshooting by up to (N-1) x estimate. The same happens across passes whenever a run outlives `PASS_SECONDS`. 'Committed' is a state the gate needs but nothing models. The fix is one owner for it: either keep a reserved total inside the pass that adds each started run's estimate, or have `standing` count the estimates of unattended runs the runner has in hand (`is_working_on`). Then add a test with two due Watches and room for only one.", "files": ["arrt/src/arrt/library/services/scheduler.py", "arrt/src/arrt/library/services/unattended.py"], "oid": "O-6"}, {"goal": "The Design Is Sound", "title": "WatchRefusal and the _LAST_RUN sentences are hand copies of sets owned elsewhere", "recommendation": "Scope: instance (two sites). (a) `WatchRefusal` restates `Refusal`'s members, and `WatchJob._refusal` converts with `WatchRefusal(str(standing.refusal))`. A `Refusal` member added later raises ValueError inside the pass, and `Scheduler.run_pass`'s broad except turns that into the whole watches job failing on every pass, seen only as `scheduler.pass_failed`. (b) `_LAST_RUN` hard-codes 'tried again within the hour' for FAILED, INTERRUPTED and HALTED_BY_BUDGET. That is a copy of `_DID_NOT_FINISH` and `RETRY_AFTER`, and the real wait is RETRY_AFTER plus up to one `PASS_SECONDS`. Following 'When a comment names a symbol as the source of truth for a set, parametrise the test over that symbol': derive the `WatchRefusal` members from `Refusal`, or parametrise a test over `Refusal` asserting each one converts. Choose the retry wording by membership in `_DID_NOT_FINISH`, or parametrise over it.", "files": ["arrt/src/arrt/library/services/watches.py", "arrt/src/arrt/library/services/scheduler.py"], "oid": "O-7"}, {"goal": "The Design Is Sound", "title": "WatchService's working_on defaults to the unsafe answer", "recommendation": "Scope: instance. `working_on: Callable[[str], bool] = lambda _run_id: False` makes 'no run is ever in flight' the default. A WatchService built without it would report a Watch with a live run as due, and the scheduler would start that Watch a second time. Only `Services.bind` passes the real callable. Make the parameter required, with no default, so a new construction site has to wire it.", "files": ["arrt/src/arrt/library/services/watches.py"], "oid": "O-8"}, {"goal": "Everything Is Coherent", "title": "observability-strategy.md still calls the scheduled-job failure row Planned, and its event tables lack the scheduler's events", "recommendation": "Scope: instance. The failure-table row at observability-strategy.md:860 still opens '*Planned, 2026-09-30; designed 2026-11-09*', and this change builds what it describes. The topic sweep and the acquisition queue each have event-table rows (`topics.sweep_wedged`, `acquisition.queue_pass`, ...). The new `scheduler.started`, `scheduler.pass`, `scheduler.pass_failed`, `scheduler.wedged`, `watch.started`, `watch.refused` and `watch.could_not_start` have none. An operator reading that artifact to learn what a stopped scheduler looks like gets told that it does not exist yet. Mark the row built, and add the event rows in the same shape the sweep's rows use.", "files": ["arrt/src/arrt/library/services/scheduler.py"], "oid": "O-9"}, {"goal": "Decisions Were Deliberate", "title": "Mid-build decisions of Chunk 04, and what settled each, for the owner", "recommendation": "Scope: none. Recorded in the plan: (1) the unattended model goes per call through WorkListRequest.model, not through a second engine, settled by 'do it right'. (2) In flight means DiscoveryRunner.is_working_on, not a non-terminal status, found by the suite, and the plan says the goals did not foresee it. (3) PASS_SECONDS=300, marked Inferred. (4) could_not_start becomes a fifth refusal. (5) __main__'s schedule=True is untested, accepted. Not recorded anywhere but code comments, and all three are what the owner reads on the Watch's sentence: halted_by_budget counts as did-not-finish and is retried within the hour (_DID_NOT_FINISH); a cancelled run waits the full interval as a completed one does; RETRY_AFTER is one hour, which is equal to an hourly Watch's own interval, so for hourly 'retry soon' does nothing. Add these as one line each among the plan's Chunk 04 decisions, or leave them if the owner accepts code-only. Separately, a Watch is gated on phase1_estimate_usd, the engine model's estimate, even when unattended_model names a different and possibly dearer model. The plan says 'standing(phase1 estimate)' but never says that the estimate ignores the model. A household that picks an expensive unattended model can go past its allowance or cap by one run's difference. State it as a decision, or price the estimate per model.", "files": ["arrt/src/arrt/library/services/watches.py", "arrt/src/arrt/library/services/scheduler.py"], "oid": "O-10"}, {"goal": "The System Can Be Understood", "title": "A run that starts but whose record_started write fails is started again at every pass", "recommendation": "WatchJob._start catches only ServiceError from runner.start. If runner.start succeeds and record_started then raises (a store error), the exception leaves run_pass and is logged as scheduler.pass_failed, but the Watch's last_attempt_at and last_run_id are never written. The next pass, five minutes later, sees the Watch as due and not in flight and starts another paid run. Spend is bounded by the cap and the allowance, because both read spend through runs.watch_id and initiated_by. The log says only 'a scheduled job's pass failed', and nothing ties it to the runs it started. A likely fix: log the started run's id together with any failure to record it (or record the attempt before starting), so the repeat is visible and bounded by the retry interval rather than by the pass interval. The same exit skips every Watch after the failing one in that pass. Scope: instance.", "files": ["arrt/src/arrt/library/services/scheduler.py"], "oid": "O-11"}, {"goal": "The System Can Be Understood", "title": "One unreadable stored last_refusal stops every Watch's pass and the standing read", "recommendation": "_sentence does `_REFUSED[WatchRefusal(watch.last_refusal)]`. A stored value outside the enum, for example one written by a later release before a rollback, raises ValueError inside standing(). That breaks due() for every Watch, so the whole job fails every pass with only scheduler.pass_failed in the log, and the screen fails too. Chunk 02 settled the same shape for settings: a stored value that no longer holds is set aside and says why. Applying that here would make a bad row fail by name for its own Watch only. The same applies to WatchRefusal(str(standing.refusal)) in WatchJob._refusal: if Refusal ever gains a member that WatchRefusal does not mirror, the result is the same pass-wide failure. A test parametrised over Refusal would pin it. Scope: class (enum reads of stored or upstream values in watches.py and scheduler.py).", "files": ["arrt/src/arrt/library/services/watches.py", "arrt/src/arrt/library/services/scheduler.py"], "oid": "O-12"}, {"goal": "The System Can Be Understood", "title": "A stopped scheduler shows as overdue only after due plus a whole cadence: up to two weeks for a weekly Watch", "recommendation": "overdue matches the plan ('due more than one cadence ago'), so the code conforms. The consequence is that with only weekly Watches, a dead scheduler thread does not show in the browser, the only alerting channel the owner chose, for 1 to 2 weeks. The scheduler.pass log line is there every five minutes, but nobody reads it under browser-only alerting. If that lag is not intended, reckon overdue from the scheduler's last pass (one shared liveness timestamp) rather than per Watch. Otherwise record the lag beside the browser-only ruling. Scope: instance.", "files": ["arrt/src/arrt/library/services/watches.py"], "oid": "O-13"}], "duration_seconds": 480, "scope": "watches", "scope_chosen_by": "binding", "scope_unresolved_cause": null, "scope_reason": null, "base_extended_from": "b5d3bf9b0a2246fb344880487731a99bf720b2a8", "chunks": ["04"], "chunks_proposed": [], "chunk": "04", "base_reviewed": null, "record_lint": {"records": [".prawduct/artifacts/build-plan-watches.md", ".prawduct/artifacts/data-model.md"], "chunk_graded": "04", "chunks_graded": ["04"], "plan_graded": ".prawduct/artifacts/build-plan-watches.md", "findings": [{"check": "chunk-ref-missing", "path": "chunk 04", "line": 282, "detail": "declared deliverable `http/static/screens/activity.js` file does not exist"}], "unchecked": [], "counts": {"chunk-ref-missing": 1, "governed-by-gap": 0, "suite-total-claim": 0, "learnings-over-budget": 0, "learnings-budget-unreasoned": 0, "learnings-core-raise-unapproved": 0, "learnings-rule-too-long": 0, "learnings-rule-body": 0, "learnings-area-dead": 0, "change-fragment": 0, "retired-claim-survives": 0}}, "dispatched_at": "2026-11-09T22:16:42Z"}}

